        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSuperb C. 32.5 Acre Residential Farm in 2 Roadside Parcels. Excellent Meadowlands in 6 Practically Sized Fields Complete with a 3 Bed Bungalow, Yard Range of Quality Outbuildings. C. 6km to Bawnboy Village. Folio's CN23998 LM17775. For Sale by Private Treaty in One or More Lots.\n\n \n\nComprised of 2 adjoining folio's, CN23998 LM17775, this quality residential farm has excellent potential in the right hands and is suitable for any agricultural equine business. Can be sold in 1 or more lots.\n\n \n\nWith over just over 300 metres frontage onto the public road, this 32.5 acre holding is divided by same into a 6.3 acre hillside meadow with the remaining 26.2 acres divided between 5 further meadows, the farmhouse adjoining yard.\n\n \n\nThe bungalow retains the traditional deep set windows on the walls formed from the original cottage and has living accommodation extending to C. 85 sqm comprising;\n\nPorch area (1.0 x 1.0), Living room ( 4.2 x 3.7) with solid fuel stove, Sitting room/diner (3.7 x 3.4) with bay window, Kitchen (3.0 x 2.7), Hallway (4.0 x 1.0), Bedroom 1 (4.0 x 2.6) with slide robe hot press, Lobby (1.6 x 1.0), Bedroom 2 (3.3 x 2.9), Bedroom 3 (4.0 x 2.1) Bathroom (3.0 x 1.8) with separate shower.\n\n \n\nThe house requires cosmetic modernisation can be extended a further 20 square metres to rear, exempt from planning permission.\n\n \n\nOriginally a stone cottage constructed around 1900 later extended to its current configuration using more standard block construction. Completed with a plaster dash exterior finish, slate roof uPVC double glazed windows. Would qualify for the SEAI Property Grants potentially other Property Refurbishment Grants.\n\n \n\nServiced by; Private well, electrical connection, dual central heating (oil solid fuel) septic tank. Fibre broadband enabled area. Bungalow BER: G.\n\n \n\nSome potential for one-off residential sites (subject to planning permission).\n\n \n\nThe yard, located to the rear of the bungalow has a divided holding yard and over 320 square metres of good quality outbuildings including a 5 bay dry shed (23.5 x 9.4) with feed pass, covered treatment yard, multiple pens GP sheds (Plan dimensions available).\n\n \n\nA fantastic opportunity for those seeking a ready to go start in farming, equestrian buyers or those already in farming looking to enlarge their current holdings. For sale in 1 or more lots.\n\n \n\nSet in a scenic area along the Cavan/Leitrim County border, only 5.8km to the village of Bawnboy (N87). Wider amenities are located at the Towns of Ballinamore (8.3km) Ballyconnell, (12.2km). Cavan Town is 30 minutes by car while Carrick-on-Shannon Enniskillen are both 40 minutes drive. GPS: 54.08714, -7.722664.\n\n \n\nViewing Highly Recommended by Appointment Only. \n\n \n\nGuide Price: POA.\n\n"
      },
